LICENCE
=======

Copyright (c) Bristol Centre for Supercomputing (BriCS).

This repository contains material under more than one licence. The licence
that applies to each skill is stated in the `license` field of the YAML
frontmatter of that skill's `SKILL.md` file, under
`site/plugins/isambard/skills/<skill-name>/`. That declaration takes
precedence over this file. The terms below summarise the position.


1. Documentation-derived skills: CC BY-SA 4.0
---------------------------------------------

Skills whose `license` field reads "CC-BY-SA-4.0" contain Markdown and image
content derived from https://docs.isambard.ac.uk/ and are licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence
(CC BY-SA 4.0):

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode

Attribution: "Markdown/image content derived from https://docs.isambard.ac.uk/,
(c) Bristol Centre for Supercomputing (BriCS)."

If you adapt or redistribute this content you must give appropriate credit,
indicate any changes made, and distribute your contributions under the same
licence.

At the time of writing this applies to the following skills:

    containers, cuda, data-transfer, getting-support, modules, mpi, nccl,
    python, slurm, spack


2. Policy skill: proprietary
----------------------------

The skill `brics-hpc-ai-code` describes BriCS policy and acceptable-use
requirements. It is NOT licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0 and is not open licensed.
It is proprietary to BriCS, and its terms are those published at:

    https://docs.isambard.ac.uk/policies/

No right to copy, modify or redistribute this skill is granted except as
those terms allow or as BriCS otherwise permits in writing. Using the skill
with the Isambard services does not alter the policies it describes; the
published BriCS policies remain authoritative.


3. All other files
------------------

Files not covered by section 1 or 2 (for example workflow scripts, agent
definitions and site or plugin configuration) carry no separate licence
declaration. No licence is granted for them by this file, and all rights are
reserved by BriCS except as the law permits.


4. Adding or changing a skill
-----------------------------

Every skill must declare its licence in its `SKILL.md` frontmatter (this is
checked by `.github/workflows/scripts/check_skill_frontmatter.py`). When a
skill is added, or its licence changes, update the lists in sections 1 and 2.


5. No warranty
--------------

Content is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. Always check the
current documentation at https://docs.isambard.ac.uk/ before relying on it.
